.TH tapectl-stage-create 1  "tapectl-stage-create " 
.SH NAME
tapectl\-stage\-create \- Create staged slices (validate → dar → encrypt → checksums)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtapectl stage create\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-\-home\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fINAME\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Create staged slices (validate → dar → encrypt → checksums)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output in JSON format
.TP
\fB\-\-version\fR \fI<VERSION>\fR
Re\-stage a specific snapshot version instead of the latest unstaged one — for when `staging clean` already released the first stage set\*(Aqs slices and another copy is wanted (issue #53). Refuses if a stage set for that version already has live slices; use `volume write` to consume them, or `staging clean` to release them first
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show what would be done without making changes
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Enable verbose output
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip confirmation prompts
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<CONFIG>\fR
Path to config file.

NOTE: on its own this ALSO relocates the whole tapectl home to the config file\*(Aqs parent directory — database, keys, staging, receipts. That is how every test harness gets an isolated home, so it still works, but it is surprising enough that it now warns. Use \-\-home when you mean "operate on a different archive", and \-\-config only to point at a config file inside that home (issue #109).
.TP
\fB\-\-home\fR \fI<HOME>\fR
tapectl home directory: database, keys, catalogs, receipts, logs.

Defaults to ~/.tapectl. The config file is taken from <home>/config.toml unless \-\-config overrides it. Also settable as TAPECTL_HOME (issue #109).
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fINAME\fR>
Unit name
